## Findings

All paths below are in `/Users/trang.doan/Desktop/code/discourse-graph/.claude/worktrees/eng-2478-add-a-type-filter-panel-to-the-obsidian-node/`.

---

### 1. `NodeTypeFilterMenu` — props, state, what it renders

`apps/obsidian/src/components/NodeTypeFilterMenu.tsx` defines **three** components; only the last is exported.

**Exported `NodeTypeFilterMenu` props** (inline type, no named interface):

```ts
export const NodeTypeFilterMenu = ({
  app, isOpen, nodeTypes, onOpenChange, onSelectedNodeTypeIdsChange, selectedNodeTypeIds,
}: {
  app: App;
  isOpen: boolean;
  nodeTypes: DiscourseNode[];
  onOpenChange: (isOpen: boolean) => void;
  onSelectedNodeTypeIdsChange: (ids: string[]) => void;
  selectedNodeTypeIds: string[];
}): ReactElement
```

Fully controlled: open state and selection both live in the caller. Its own state is only `useMemo` derivations (`allTypeIds`, `isFilterActive`, `panelSelectedIds`, `activeFilterCount`) — no `useState`.

**It renders both the trigger button and the panel**, because it returns a `<SearchDropdown>` (`apps/obsidian/src/components/SearchDropdown.tsx`) with `iconName="filter"`, `panelClassName="w-64"`, `badgeCount={activeFilterCount}`, `isDisabled={nodeTypes.length === 0}`. The caller does **not** supply the button. `SearchDropdown` renders:

```tsx
<div ref={containerRef} className="relative shrink-0" onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}>
  <button ... className={`clickable-icon relative ${isOpen || isActive ? "is-active" : ""}`}>
```

so the panel is absolutely positioned relative to `SearchDropdown`'s own `relative` wrapper div:

```tsx
className={`border-modifier-border absolute right-0 top-full z-50 mt-1 overflow-hidden rounded-md border bg-primary shadow-[shadow:var(--shadow-s)] outline-none ${panelClassName}`}
```

i.e. right-aligned, directly below the trigger, `z-50`.

`NodeTypeFilterPanel` (inner, not exported) is the only piece with real local state: `const [query, setQuery] = useState("")` plus `searchRef`, and it auto-focuses the search box when `showTypeSearch`. `NodeTypeFilterRow` (inner, not exported) is a stateless row.

Note: `SearchDropdown` is not purely presentational — it pushes an Obsidian `Scope` for Escape (`app.keymap.pushScope`), installs an `activeDocument` capture-phase `mousedown` outside-click closer, and implements ArrowUp/ArrowDown roving focus + Tab-closes. Its `handleKeyDown` calls `event.stopPropagation()` with the comment "Panel keystrokes must not reach the modal's Enter and arrow result navigation".

---

### 2. "Select all", "All selected", "Only"

- **There is no "Select all" and no "All selected" label.** The code explicitly rejects a select-all control:

```tsx
{/* Clearing is the only thing this control ever does, so it says so and
    appears only when there is a filter to clear. A "select all" checkbox
    would sit checked-and-inert whenever no filter is active, since an empty
    selection and a full one are the same state. */}
{isFilterActive && (
  <div className="border-modifier-border border-b p-2">
    <button type="button" onClick={(event) => { ... onSelectedIdsChange([]); }} ...>
      {`Clear filter (${selectedIds.length})`}
    </button>
  </div>
)}
```

  The only summary surface is the trigger's `badgeCount` and the aria label `` `Filter by type, ${activeFilterCount} selected` ``.

- **"Only" on hover exists**, in `NodeTypeFilterRow`:

```tsx
<button
  type="button"
  // Pointer-only: arrow keys stop once per row, on the checkbox.
  tabIndex={-1}
  // Hidden until the row is hovered so the list stays scannable.
  className="text-muted hover:text-normal shrink-0 opacity-0 transition-opacity group-hover:opacity-100"
  onClick={(event) => { event.stopPropagation(); onSelectOnly(); }}
  onMouseDown={(event) => event.preventDefault()}
>
  Only
</button>
```

  wired as `onSelectOnly={() => onSelectedIdsChange([nodeType.id])}`.

- **"Only" does NOT collapse the panel.** It only calls `onSelectedIdsChange`; nothing calls `onOpenChange(false)`. The panel stays open (the `onMouseDown` preventDefault also keeps focus from moving).

---

### 3. `discourseNodeTypeFilter.ts` exports

`apps/obsidian/src/utils/discourseNodeTypeFilter.ts` — **100% pure, zero React** (its only import is the `DiscourseNode` type). All hook/DOM coupling lives in the component file.

| Export | Signature | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `NODE_TYPE_FILTER_SEARCH_THRESHOLD` | `= 7` | Above this many types the panel adds a search box. Comment: "the modal is desktop-only". |
| `hasActiveTypeFilter` | `({ selectedTypeIds: string[]; allTypeIds: string[] }) => boolean` | `len > 0 && len < allTypeIds.length` |
| `toPanelSelectedIds` | `({ selectedTypeIds, allTypeIds }) => string[]` | Maps no-filter (`[]`) to all ids so the panel shows every row checked |
| `fromPanelSelectedIds` | `({ panelSelectedIds, allTypeIds }) => string[]` | Collapses both empty and full back to `[]` (no filter) |
| `filterNodeTypesByQuery` | `(nodeTypes: DiscourseNode[], query: string) => DiscourseNode[]` | Case-insensitive, trimmed `name.includes` substring match |

Module doc comment:

```
 * Node type filtering for the search modal. An empty `selectedTypeIds` means no
 * filter, matching `filterCandidatesByNodeTypeIds` in QueryEngine — so "nothing
 * selected" and "every type selected" are the same state and both show all nodes.
 * Ported from Roam's advanced search so both apps filter alike.
```

**There is no `__tests__` file for this module.** `apps/obsidian/src/utils/__tests__/` contains 20 test files, none of them `discourseNodeTypeFilter.test.ts`; grep for every exported symbol finds no other reference anywhere in `apps/obsidian/src` besides `NodeTypeFilterMenu.tsx` itself. (A separate `apps/roam/src/utils/discourseNodeTypeFilter.ts` exists — same name, different app.)

---

### 4. `NodeSearchModal` wiring

`apps/obsidian/src/components/NodeSearchModal.tsx`:

- **State lives in the modal body component** (line 376), initialised empty — i.e. *no* types checked in state, which the panel renders as all-checked:

```ts
// Single source of truth: ENG-2111's tag chips will read and write this too.
const [selectedNodeTypeIds, setSelectedNodeTypeIds] = useState<string[]>([]);
// One value per toolbar, so two panels can never be open at once.
const [openDropdown, setOpenDropdown] = useState<SearchDropdownId>(null);
```

- `SearchDropdownId = "type-filter" | "sort" | "display-options" | null` is exported from `SearchDropdown.tsx` and arbitrates mutual exclusion across three menus.
- **Two consumers share the same setter**: `NodeTypeChipsSearchInput` (line ~658) and `NodeTypeFilterMenu` (line 664) both get `onSelectedNodeTypeIdsChange={setSelectedNodeTypeIds}` and `selectedNodeTypeIds`.
- Open/close goes through:

```ts
const handleDropdownOpenChange = ({ id, isOpen }): void => {
  setOpenDropdown(isOpen ? id : null);
  // Returns the keyboard path to the results the moment the panel closes.
  if (!isOpen) inputRef.current?.focus();
};
```

- **No explicit reset exists.** Selection resets only because `NodeSearchModal extends Modal` creates a fresh React root in `onOpen()` (`createRoot(contentEl)`) and calls `this.root.unmount()` in `onClose()`.
- Selected ids reach ranking in the `results` memo:

```ts
const ranked = rankDiscourseNodesByTitle({
  candidates: [...nodesState.nodes, ...tagCandidates],
  query: debouncedQuery,
  nodeTypeIds: selectedNodeTypeIds,
});
```

  then `sortSearchResults(...)`, `.slice(0, MAX_VISIBLE_RESULTS)`, then a `flatMap` that drops results whose `nodeTypeId` is missing from `nodeTypesById`.
- Toolbar row container: `<div className="flex items-start gap-2 px-1 pt-1">`, with the comment "Padded so a trigger's count badge is not clipped by the modal's overflow-hidden content."

---

### 5. `rankDiscourseNodesByTitle`

`apps/obsidian/src/services/QueryEngine.ts:816`:

```ts
export const rankDiscourseNodesByTitle = ({
  candidates, query, nodeTypeIds,
}: {
  candidates: SearchableNode[];
  query: string;
  nodeTypeIds?: string[];
}): RankedDiscourseNode[] => {
  const filtered = filterCandidatesByNodeTypeIds(candidates, nodeTypeIds);
  ...
```

Filtering happens **before** scoring (doc comment at line 812-815: "Best match first, uncapped — capping is the caller's… Filters before scoring: same results, less work."). The helper (line 800):

```ts
const filterCandidatesByNodeTypeIds = (
  candidates: SearchableNode[],
  nodeTypeIds?: string[],
): SearchableNode[] => {
  if (!nodeTypeIds?.length) return candidates;
  const selected = new Set(nodeTypeIds);
  return candidates.filter((candidate) => selected.has(candidate.nodeTypeId));
};
```

**`undefined` and `[]` are identical** — both mean "no filter, return everything" (`!nodeTypeIds?.length`). That is why `fromPanelSelectedIds` can safely collapse "all checked" to `[]`.

Empty query is not an empty result: it returns everything sorted by `title.localeCompare` then `nodesFirst` (real nodes before tag candidates), with a synthetic `match: { score: 0, matches: [] }`. Non-empty query uses Obsidian `prepareFuzzySearch` and sorts by `b.match.score - a.match.score || nodesFirst(a, b)`. Results are uncapped.

`SearchableNode = { file: TFile; title: string; nodeTypeId: string; tagLine?: { line: number; tag: string } }`; `RankedDiscourseNode = SearchableNode & { match: SearchResult }`.

